dings.readable and findings.reason for a TERMINAL `failed` plan-review job (no verdict/sidecar), e.g. readable=false with a dedicated reason such as `run-failed`, and add an AC covering it.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Disposition enumerates: 'current-review-result-sidecar is readable. sidecar-not-emitted ..., review-result-generation-unknown, and run-stale-running are unavailable. review-result-sidecar-missing covers ... run-running and run-attaching mean keep polling.' — no entry for a terminal `failed` job.","AC: 'Assert non-terminal plan-review runs report findings.readable=false, reason=\"run-<status>\", and reviewed_at=null.' — scoped to NON-terminal only; a `failed` run is terminal.","src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py:139-140 `_terminal_from_result`: an error result returns status `failed`; src/rebar/llm/gate_runs.py:131 returns the recorded terminal status (which may be `failed`)."],"finding":"The findings.reason vocabulary has no mapping for a TERMINAL `failed` plan-review job (a gate/LLM error that settled the run with no verdict and no sidecar). `_terminal_from_result` classifies an error-bearing result as status `failed`, and `_resolve_status` returns `failed` as a settled/terminal status. The AC clause `reason=\"run-<status>\"` applies only to NON-terminal runs, and the Disposition enumerates reasons for sidecar-missing / not-emitted / generation-unknown / running / attaching / stale-running but never for a terminal `failed` run — so an executor cannot derive what findings.readable and findings.reason to emit when a plan-review job failed.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1a2de494b3444cde","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan step 6-7 + 'Disposition' paragraph; Acceptance Criteria line 'non-terminal plan-review runs report ... reason=\"run-<status>\"'","norm_id":"nbe1e3c063b1fff27","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"sc